challenges.description:
Which interface best represents a typed HTTP client for software engineers use?

  A)  interface Client { request(url: string): any }
  B)  interface Client { get<T>(url: string): Promise<T>; post<T>(url: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> }
  C)  interface Client { fetch: typeof fetch }
  D)  interface Client { url: string; method: string }

What advantage does this typed logger have over console.log?

  interface LogEntry { level: 'info' | 'warn' | 'error'; message: string; timestamp: string; fields?: Record<string, unknown> }
  function log(entry: LogEntry): void { console.log(JSON.stringify(entry)) }
